   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to information\nconcerning services for human trafficking victims",
    "basePrintNo": "S5527",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5527-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1266-m, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5527\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to information\nconcerning services for human trafficking victims\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo require MTA facilities to provide information concerning services for\nhuman trafficking victims.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends the Public Authorities law to require the posting of information\nconcerning services for human trafficking victims within MTA facilities.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nHuman trafficking is a global phenomenon that generates $150 billion in\nannual profits as well as ruins lives and communities. In 2021, an esti-\nmated 25 million people were trafficked. The convenience and anonymity\nof much of public transit makes it convenient for traffickers to move\nvictims.\n\nBecause transportation terminals are known hubs used to traffic victims,\nthey are an ideal location to provide information about victim services.\nThis information can not only inform victims, but also other travelers\nabout the availability of services. This legislation will afford victims\naccess to the tools and resources to hopefully escape their captors.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA.10248a of 2021 and 2022, referred to corporations, authorities, and\ncommissions. Same as 5.8679, passed senate.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the sixtieth day after it shall have\nbecome law.\n",
